"Refinement (user example): a 10-cookie quest may have indexes 0-2 GUARANTEED in map A, 3-5 guaranteed in map B, and 6-9 ELIGIBLE in either. So per map per quest: guaranteedIndexes (must spawn here; an index is guaranteed in at most ONE map) + eligibleIndexes (may spawn here; shareable across maps, rng decides per generation). Shared eligible indexes may physically spawn in several maps/instances -- SAFE by construction: supply is limited by BITS, not physical items; eating one sets the bit and every duplicate then smells off to that player, popcount caps the grant. Push-time validation: an index appears as guaranteed at most once globally, guaranteed and eligible sets never overlap for the same quest, all indexes < bitCount."